Copperhead Firetower and Bear Lake Trail		Hiking				Scioto	Ohio Department of Natural Resources, Division of Forestry					A trail within Shawnee State Forest providing access to the Copperhead Fire Tower (Ohio's first fire tower, 1924; ODNR Historic Site #6) and Bear Lake. The approach climbs Copperhead Hill to an elevation exceeding 1,200 feet.		Parent: Shawnee State Forest (SC-S-0004 pending). Named trail documented on AllTrails. Trail provides access to Copperhead Fire Tower (SC-S-0010 pending). Trail name is the AllTrails community name; ODNR formal trail name not confirmed — may match or differ. Bear Lake is a small forest lake near the horsemen's campground. Length and difficulty not confirmed.			https://www.alltrails.com/trail/us/ohio/copperhead-firetower-and-bear-lake	SC-T-0009
