River Otter Trail		Hiking			1.5	Scioto	Ohio Department of Natural Resources, Division of Natural Areas and Preserves					A 1.5-mile linear loop trail located on the east side of Tatman-Coe Road in Union Township, running along the north bank of Scioto Brush Creek. The trail affords excellent views of the deep pools in the creek that lie within the preserve. The preserve offers excellent birding in all seasons, particularly during migration.		TIER 2 MISS — discovered during Tier 4 county research via Scenic Scioto Heritage Trail website. Not in baseline seeds. Trail located at Tatman-Coe Road, Union Township — same address as Scioto Brush Creek State Nature Preserve (SC-S-0008). Trail is within the preserve (source: Scioto Heritage Trail page states 'the deep pools in the creek that lie within the preserve'). Parent: Scioto Brush Creek State Nature Preserve (SC-S-0008 pending). Length 1.5 miles confirmed by source.				SC-T-0026
Allan W. Eckert Trail		Hiking				Scioto	Scioto County (County Commissioners / Scioto County Parks Department)					A walking and biking trail at Earl Thomas Conley Riverside Park offering views of the banks and bottom lands at the confluence of the Scioto and Ohio Rivers.		Named trail within Earl Thomas Conley Riverside Park (Tier 4). Trail named after Allan W. Eckert, prolific Ohio historical author. Trail length not confirmed. Parent: Earl Thomas Conley Riverside Park. Sources describe it as offering 'a view of the banks and bottom lands at the confluence of the Scioto and the Ohio Rivers.'				SC-T-0027
